1
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:12,033
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,833 --> 00:00:33,000
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,333 --> 00:00:35,300
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:41,367
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:44,233
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,233 --> 00:00:45,400
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:46,367
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,867
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,333 --> 00:00:51,433
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,767 --> 00:00:53,933
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,933 --> 00:00:55,667
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,833 --> 00:00:58,267
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,267 --> 00:01:00,600
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,233 --> 00:01:03,400
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:06,600
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,433 --> 00:01:09,700
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,267 --> 00:01:11,933
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,933 --> 00:01:13,133
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,133 --> 00:01:14,833
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,933 --> 00:01:22,267
<i>You successfully
turned over the evidence.</i>

21
00:01:22,267 --> 00:01:25,000
<i>- Good work.
- Armed men ambushed us.</i>

22
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,567
<i>They even held
Lt. Jacinto hostage.</i>

23
00:01:26,567 --> 00:01:27,867
<i>- Argh!
- Shush!</i>

24
00:01:27,867 --> 00:01:29,133
<i> But they managed to escape.</i>

25
00:01:29,133 --> 00:01:31,700
<i>For sure, the Zafras did this
because it's their gold!</i>

26
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:33,267
<i> A bag of jewelry is missing.</i>

27
00:01:33,267 --> 00:01:35,833
<i>- No second chances.
- Hear me out.</i>

28
00:01:35,833 --> 00:01:38,233
<i>I risked my life
just to get this.</i>

29
00:01:38,233 --> 00:01:40,133
<i>- Take him out!
- Gabo!</i>

30
00:01:40,133 --> 00:01:41,200
<i> Gabo!</i>

31
00:01:41,233 --> 00:01:43,967
<i>Let's go all out!
Even if we die!</i>

32
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,133
<i>- Help him up!
- Somebody help us!</i>

33
00:01:47,133 --> 00:01:48,233
<i> Gabo's hurt!</i>

34
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:50,133
<i>- Who did you fight?
- They're looking for someone.</i>

35
00:01:50,133 --> 00:01:51,500
I think they're the ones looking
<i> for Gloria!</i>

36
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:53,467
<i>This happened to Gabo
because of her!</i>

37
00:01:53,467 --> 00:01:55,000
<i> I can't think straight.</i>

38
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,100
<i> I'm hiding here in your home</i>

39
00:01:57,100 --> 00:02:01,233
<i>because I know you're the key
to clearing my name.</i>

40
00:02:01,233 --> 00:02:03,333
<i>But I am getting to know
who you are.</i>

41
00:02:03,333 --> 00:02:05,267
<i> I hope I was wrong about you.</i>

42
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:13,200
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

43
00:02:17,633 --> 00:02:19,833
[SAM] <i> A lot of people
</i> are getting involved...

44
00:02:20,467 --> 00:02:24,300
<i>...in my search for evidence
against Victor Zafra.</i>

45
00:02:24,933 --> 00:02:28,267
<i>And they won't stop
until they kill me.</i>

46
00:02:33,533 --> 00:02:34,733
[OBJECTS CLATTERING]

47
00:02:34,733 --> 00:02:37,100
<i> I have to find a way...</i>

48
00:02:37,967 --> 00:02:40,133
...to make them think I'm dead.

49
00:02:40,133 --> 00:02:47,067
[MUSIC TURNS DRAMATIC]

50
00:02:54,333 --> 00:02:56,900
[MUSIC TURNS STIRRING]

51
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:59,133
I can't just confuse the Zafras.

52
00:02:59,833 --> 00:03:02,767
<i>Even if I lure them away
from Ginintuang Lupa...</i>

53
00:03:02,767 --> 00:03:04,900
...people will still get dragged
<i> into this mess.</i>

54
00:03:06,367 --> 00:03:08,367
<i> They need to stop searching.</i>

55
00:03:09,033 --> 00:03:15,933
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

56
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:22,200
[TIRES SCREECHING]

57
00:03:22,233 --> 00:03:23,767
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

58
00:03:23,767 --> 00:03:27,933
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

59
00:03:27,933 --> 00:03:29,033
[CAR DOOR SHUTS]

60
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:33,800
[DEBORAH] Let me guess.
The plan failed.

61
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:35,800
They couldn't retrieve
all of the gold.

62
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:37,467
Paquito's son failed.

63
00:03:37,467 --> 00:03:40,000
Pa, you should've let me do it.

64
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,467
Who are those failures
you hired, anyway?

65
00:03:42,467 --> 00:03:44,667
Don't question my decision!

66
00:03:45,433 --> 00:03:48,500
Those men you call failures
are veterans in fighting

67
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:51,300
by just using their strategies
and skills alone.

68
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:55,400
[DEBORAH] Mariano,
Lucas just wanted to help.

69
00:03:55,433 --> 00:03:57,333
Pa, I should've handled it!

70
00:03:58,200 --> 00:03:59,467
You want to help?

71
00:04:00,233 --> 00:04:02,233
Then keep your mouth shut!

72
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:06,467
You've got a long way to go
before reaching my level,

73
00:04:06,467 --> 00:04:08,600
so don't speak for me.

74
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:09,900
It's easy to act tough...

75
00:04:11,167 --> 00:04:12,867
...when you're not
in an actual fight.

76
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:21,433
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

77
00:04:25,433 --> 00:04:28,667
[TOTO] Here, come in.
Ma'am, you have a visitor!

78
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:31,467
[ISOBEL GASPS]

79
00:04:32,267 --> 00:04:33,300
Max!

80
00:04:33,300 --> 00:04:35,533
What happened to you?
Why do you look like that?

81
00:04:35,533 --> 00:04:38,433
- Do you have any injuries?
- I'm okay, Auntie.

82
00:04:38,433 --> 00:04:39,500
I'm fine, Mom.

83
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:43,100
What happened? What's this?
Can you explain?

84
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:45,900
[UMALI] Ma'am, we had
a small encounter

85
00:04:45,900 --> 00:04:47,533
with some bad men.

86
00:04:47,533 --> 00:04:51,067
- But we quickly saved Max.
- Saved?!

87
00:04:51,067 --> 00:04:53,900
Toto, call your Sir Ricardo
right now!

88
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:55,600
- Yes!
- Ma.

89
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:58,633
- I'm okay!
- No!

90
00:04:58,633 --> 00:05:00,500
Your dad needs to know
about this.

91
00:05:01,633 --> 00:05:02,700
[KNOCKS]

92
00:05:03,333 --> 00:05:06,800
Sir, the NLEA officers are back.

93
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:10,567
It looks like they have
good news.

94
00:05:10,567 --> 00:05:12,100
They even came here personally.

95
00:05:17,333 --> 00:05:18,633
[MAX] Mom.

96
00:05:18,633 --> 00:05:20,567
- [RICARDO] Domingo.
- Sir.

97
00:05:21,267 --> 00:05:22,533
How was the transfer?

98
00:05:24,733 --> 00:05:25,833
Max.

99
00:05:25,833 --> 00:05:27,067
You were together?

100
00:05:27,567 --> 00:05:29,300
They came back together.

101
00:05:30,133 --> 00:05:32,267
They were all there
during the encounter.

102
00:05:34,433 --> 00:05:36,167
Encounter? What happened?

103
00:05:36,167 --> 00:05:40,800
Sir, we came here personally
to explain what happened.

104
00:05:41,333 --> 00:05:44,667
We were attacked by masked men.

105
00:05:45,167 --> 00:05:47,733
They were after the gold.

106
00:05:47,967 --> 00:05:49,500
And? Did you catch them?

107
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:53,267
- Did you secure the gold?
- Sir...

108
00:05:53,267 --> 00:05:56,200
They took Lieutenant Jacinto
hostage.

109
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:57,633
You brought Max with you?!

110
00:05:57,633 --> 00:05:59,200
- Dad, I insisted.
- Hey!

111
00:06:00,733 --> 00:06:03,200
[DOMINGO] The gold's secured.
Most of it.

112
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:05,233
The criminals got away
with one bag of gold,

113
00:06:05,233 --> 00:06:07,200
but the rest is safe now.

114
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:08,400
Because of what happened,

115
00:06:08,433 --> 00:06:10,567
we had to choose Max
over the gold.

116
00:06:10,567 --> 00:06:13,700
So now we're supposed
to be grateful to you for this?

117
00:06:13,700 --> 00:06:14,767
[RICARDO HUFFS]

118
00:06:16,367 --> 00:06:17,533
- Get out.
- General...

119
00:06:17,533 --> 00:06:18,633
Get out!

120
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,367
Yes, sir.

121
00:06:20,367 --> 00:06:21,467
[UMALI] Sir.

122
00:06:23,700 --> 00:06:25,267
Take that straight to the vault.

123
00:06:25,267 --> 00:06:26,367
Yes, sir.

124
00:06:29,467 --> 00:06:32,033
What else do you want
Lucas to do, huh?

125
00:06:32,033 --> 00:06:34,633
He's already succeeded
with Samanta Jacinto.

126
00:06:34,633 --> 00:06:39,033
He wants to prove to you
that he can do what Victor does.

127
00:06:39,033 --> 00:06:43,033
He'll never be like Victor.

128
00:06:43,067 --> 00:06:45,800
Well, he doesn't have
to be like Victor.

129
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:47,333
Victor is Victor.

130
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:49,367
Lucas is Lucas.

131
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:52,667
But I've given him
plenty of chances already.

132
00:06:53,267 --> 00:06:54,367
Look...

133
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,533
I know he grew up privileged.

134
00:06:57,533 --> 00:07:00,233
He grew up a Zafra,
and being a Zafra means power.

135
00:07:00,233 --> 00:07:03,333
But that doesn't mean
he can't do

136
00:07:03,333 --> 00:07:05,233
what we're asking him to do.

137
00:07:06,233 --> 00:07:10,000
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

138
00:07:10,533 --> 00:07:13,133
Pacquitio's son has guts.

139
00:07:13,133 --> 00:07:14,267
He's a fighter.

140
00:07:14,867 --> 00:07:17,500
He's resourceful and fearless.

141
00:07:18,833 --> 00:07:20,767
Lucas can learn from him.

142
00:07:20,767 --> 00:07:22,467
But he messed up, right?

143
00:07:22,467 --> 00:07:24,333
But the fight isn't over yet.

144
00:07:24,967 --> 00:07:27,000
They still have a chance
to make up for it.

145
00:07:27,567 --> 00:07:28,867
Fine.

146
00:07:28,867 --> 00:07:31,267
Then let them finish
what they started.

147
00:07:31,267 --> 00:07:35,967
But this time,
Lucas has to lead them.

148
00:07:35,967 --> 00:07:38,767
I know my son has potential.

149
00:07:38,767 --> 00:07:40,767
We just haven't tapped
into it yet.

150
00:07:40,767 --> 00:07:43,733
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

151
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:47,100
You can take on
your enemies yourself,

152
00:07:47,933 --> 00:07:50,433
yet you still let Max go
into the field.

153
00:07:51,533 --> 00:07:52,667
Mom!

154
00:07:53,233 --> 00:07:54,633
That's part of my job.

155
00:07:54,633 --> 00:07:55,900
I'm with the NLEA.

156
00:07:56,767 --> 00:07:58,200
It's my job to solve the case.

157
00:07:58,200 --> 00:07:59,600
- To save...
- Shut up!

158
00:07:59,967 --> 00:08:03,533
Isobel, what matters now
is that Max is safe.

159
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:05,600
Ricardo, how long?

160
00:08:07,400 --> 00:08:12,000
How long are you willing
to risk your family's safety

161
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:14,033
just because of whatever's
going on between

162
00:08:14,033 --> 00:08:17,033
the Zafras and you
that I don't understand?!

163
00:08:17,033 --> 00:08:18,133
This is her job!

164
00:08:18,133 --> 00:08:19,900
This is what she signed up for.

165
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:21,367
Max didn't do anything wrong.

166
00:08:23,233 --> 00:08:26,000
If anyone's at fault,
it's the Zafras.

167
00:08:27,067 --> 00:08:29,700
They're the ones deliberately
provoking me.

168
00:08:29,767 --> 00:08:32,133
You can blame your enemies?

169
00:08:33,233 --> 00:08:35,033
What about your own people?

170
00:08:35,033 --> 00:08:36,833
What about the dangerous jobs

171
00:08:36,833 --> 00:08:38,500
you've put your children in?!

172
00:08:39,300 --> 00:08:40,633
You!

173
00:08:40,633 --> 00:08:44,300
Why can't you look
at yourself in the mirror?

174
00:08:44,300 --> 00:08:45,667
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

175
00:08:45,667 --> 00:08:46,767
[MUSIC STOPS]

176
00:08:46,767 --> 00:08:53,667
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

177
00:08:55,133 --> 00:08:56,233
[DOGS BARKING]

178
00:08:59,267 --> 00:09:00,300
[MAN 1] Hey!

179
00:09:00,867 --> 00:09:03,000
Take me to my real house.

180
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,800
[MAN 2] Quit making
so much noise!

181
00:09:04,800 --> 00:09:06,400
[MAN 1]
I've had too much to drink.

182
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:08,533
[MAN 2] Stop bothering
our neighbors.

183
00:09:08,533 --> 00:09:09,967
[MAN 1]
I've had too much to drink.

184
00:09:09,967 --> 00:09:11,433
That's not even my house!

185
00:09:11,433 --> 00:09:14,233
That's what you get for
drinking someone else's shot!

186
00:09:14,233 --> 00:09:16,367
[MAN 1]
You're drunk too, aren't you?

187
00:09:16,367 --> 00:09:23,233
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

188
00:09:37,300 --> 00:09:44,167
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

189
00:09:58,100 --> 00:10:04,900
[MUSIC BECOMES PENSIVE]

190
00:10:18,967 --> 00:10:25,767
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

191
00:10:26,567 --> 00:10:29,467
[GUNSHOTS]

192
00:10:29,467 --> 00:10:30,533
[DOGS BARKING]

193
00:10:30,533 --> 00:10:31,800
[DOGS HOWLING]

194
00:10:33,333 --> 00:10:36,367
[DOGS BARKING]

195
00:10:42,633 --> 00:10:43,600
Mom, I'm okay.

196
00:10:44,233 --> 00:10:45,400
- I'm fine.
- [DOOR CLOSES]

197
00:10:46,167 --> 00:10:47,300
I'm okay!

198
00:10:47,300 --> 00:10:48,500
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

199
00:10:48,500 --> 00:10:51,867
You know, if I could just
lock you up here at home

200
00:10:51,867 --> 00:10:53,600
to keep you out of danger,

201
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:54,967
I would do it.

202
00:10:58,300 --> 00:10:59,367
[SIGHS]

203
00:11:00,333 --> 00:11:02,633
Unfortunately, I need your help.

204
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:06,633
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

205
00:11:06,633 --> 00:11:08,800
To find your sister.

206
00:11:12,067 --> 00:11:13,033
[INHALES SHARPLY]

207
00:11:14,233 --> 00:11:16,233
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

208
00:11:19,167 --> 00:11:20,400
I'm sorry, Ma.

209
00:11:22,933 --> 00:11:24,200
I made you worry.

210
00:11:25,467 --> 00:11:26,567
[SIGHS]

211
00:11:26,567 --> 00:11:33,567
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

212
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,267
Rest up.

213
00:11:37,167 --> 00:11:39,533
I know you had a long day.

214
00:11:44,300 --> 00:11:51,200
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

215
00:12:03,433 --> 00:12:04,833
- [DOORKNOB SQUEAKS]
- [DOOR OPENS]

216
00:12:04,833 --> 00:12:06,333
[DANTE] Oh, Gloria.

217
00:12:06,333 --> 00:12:08,400
What were you doing outside?
It's way too late.

218
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:11,367
Sorry, I just stepped out
for some air.

219
00:12:11,367 --> 00:12:13,100
Something bad
could've happened to you,

220
00:12:13,100 --> 00:12:14,333
with so many troublemakers
around here.

221
00:12:14,733 --> 00:12:16,333
Alright, get inside now.

222
00:12:16,333 --> 00:12:19,467
You don't want
to come face-to-face

223
00:12:19,467 --> 00:12:21,133
with Gabo's enemies.

224
00:12:21,133 --> 00:12:22,433
Lock up, okay?

225
00:12:22,433 --> 00:12:24,233
Leave the patrolling to me.

226
00:12:24,233 --> 00:12:27,433
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

227
00:12:27,433 --> 00:12:28,400
[DOOR CLOSES]

228
00:12:36,333 --> 00:12:37,533
[MUSIC FADING]

229
00:12:37,533 --> 00:12:39,067
- [TWINKLE] Ma'am.
- [DOOR OPENS]

230
00:12:39,067 --> 00:12:41,000
- Yes?
- Isobel, good morning!

231
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:42,900
Oh. Hi, Pinky.

232
00:12:43,300 --> 00:12:45,400
- Why are you so early?
- Good morning.

233
00:12:45,400 --> 00:12:48,700
After hearing Sebastian's
explanation last night

234
00:12:48,733 --> 00:12:51,233
about his future plans with Sam,

235
00:12:51,233 --> 00:12:52,733
- Mm-hmm.
- I realized...

236
00:12:52,733 --> 00:12:55,500
there was someone I wanted
to introduce to you.

237
00:12:56,233 --> 00:12:57,567
Ah, really?

238
00:12:57,567 --> 00:12:58,867
What for?

239
00:12:58,867 --> 00:13:02,233
I know someone
who's capable of seeing things

240
00:13:02,233 --> 00:13:05,700
that we don't normally see.

241
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:07,567
Call it a seer,

242
00:13:07,567 --> 00:13:10,433
a fortune teller, or whatever,

243
00:13:10,433 --> 00:13:13,833
but she can give you the
answers you're looking for.

244
00:13:13,833 --> 00:13:15,233
You mean to say...

245
00:13:15,733 --> 00:13:18,000
I'll be asking for help
from a fortune teller?

246
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,133
[PINKY] Mm-hmm.

247
00:13:20,300 --> 00:13:21,700
Uh...

248
00:13:23,400 --> 00:13:24,600
[DOOR OPENS]

249
00:13:24,600 --> 00:13:28,433
[MUSIC BUILDING UP]

250
00:13:28,433 --> 00:13:30,967
[MYSTICAL MUSIC PLAYING]

251
00:13:30,967 --> 00:13:32,000
[EXHALES HEAVILY]

252
00:13:33,467 --> 00:13:34,867
Madam Rosa?

253
00:13:36,133 --> 00:13:37,400
Isobel.

254
00:13:37,400 --> 00:13:38,433
[ISOBEL GASPS]

255
00:13:40,867 --> 00:13:41,933
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

256
00:13:43,967 --> 00:13:45,567
Madam Rosa senses

257
00:13:45,567 --> 00:13:47,600
that many things are
troubling your mind.

258
00:13:48,067 --> 00:13:49,567
That there is sorrow
in your heart.

259
00:13:49,567 --> 00:13:51,167
And that you carry
countless questions.

260
00:13:51,167 --> 00:13:53,333
That's true, Madam Rosa.

261
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:55,700
But don't worry...

262
00:13:56,733 --> 00:13:59,333
Madam Rosa will answer them all.

263
00:13:59,333 --> 00:14:00,667
[MYSTICAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

264
00:14:00,667 --> 00:14:02,200
[SIGHS IN RELIEF]

265
00:14:02,267 --> 00:14:06,933
Your biggest question has
to do with one of them.

266
00:14:15,733 --> 00:14:16,967
With Sam.

267
00:14:17,467 --> 00:14:18,633
[EXHALES HEAVILY]

268
00:14:19,967 --> 00:14:21,533
You're right.
[BREATH QUIVERS]

269
00:14:22,867 --> 00:14:24,000
You're right.

270
00:14:24,667 --> 00:14:26,433
Bring me to her room.

271
00:14:26,833 --> 00:14:28,833
Yes, I'll take you there.

272
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:30,933
[ISOBEL EXHALES DEEPLY]

273
00:14:32,667 --> 00:14:33,633
[DOOR OPENS]

274
00:14:34,167 --> 00:14:35,233
[GROANS]

275
00:14:35,233 --> 00:14:36,533
Madam Rosa?

276
00:14:36,533 --> 00:14:38,900
I sense a powerful energy here.

277
00:14:38,900 --> 00:14:41,933
Many images are flowing
into Madam Rosa's mind.

278
00:14:41,933 --> 00:14:44,233
[ISOBEL] What do you see?

279
00:14:44,233 --> 00:14:45,600
Where's Sam?

280
00:14:46,433 --> 00:14:47,667
Sam?

281
00:14:47,667 --> 00:14:49,967
Sam... Sam... Sam...

282
00:14:49,967 --> 00:14:51,800
Sam is missing.

283
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:54,533
Isobel, give me
Sam's most expensive--

284
00:14:54,533 --> 00:14:57,600
precious belonging
in her room.

285
00:14:57,600 --> 00:14:58,700
Hurry up, Isobel!

286
00:14:58,700 --> 00:15:00,300
- Here you go.
- Sam, Sam...

287
00:15:00,300 --> 00:15:02,233
She holds this watch dear.

288
00:15:03,267 --> 00:15:06,933
This was given to her
by her brother RJ.

289
00:15:06,933 --> 00:15:07,933
- Is it expensive?
- What?

290
00:15:07,933 --> 00:15:09,067
Is it important to her?

291
00:15:09,067 --> 00:15:10,067
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

292
00:15:10,067 --> 00:15:12,400
She values that watch deeply.

293
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:14,067
This is worth a lot of money.

294
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:18,300
This... is very important
to Sam.

295
00:15:18,367 --> 00:15:20,233
It holds personal meaning
for her.

296
00:15:20,233 --> 00:15:22,567
[VOICE QUIVERING]

297
00:15:22,567 --> 00:15:26,567
Sam! Sam! Sam!

298
00:15:27,233 --> 00:15:29,100
- Sam...
- [SNIFFLES]

299
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:30,300
Well?
[CRYING]

300
00:15:31,800 --> 00:15:33,467
It's not working.

301
00:15:33,467 --> 00:15:34,867
What?

302
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:37,900
Madam Rosa,
what do you mean by that?

303
00:15:37,900 --> 00:15:39,433
It doesn't work at all.

304
00:15:40,367 --> 00:15:42,900
- [HUFFS]
- [SNIFFLES]

305
00:15:44,133 --> 00:15:51,067
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
INSTRUMENTAL PLAYING]

306
00:15:58,033 --> 00:15:59,067
[EXHALES SOFTLY]

307
00:16:01,067 --> 00:16:04,367
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

308
00:16:04,367 --> 00:16:05,500
Gloria, dear...

309
00:16:05,767 --> 00:16:07,233
H-How's my son doing?

310
00:16:08,100 --> 00:16:09,767
He's getting better.

311
00:16:11,367 --> 00:16:12,867
[RUDY] Were you able to rest?

312
00:16:12,867 --> 00:16:14,033
Any sleep at all?

313
00:16:14,533 --> 00:16:17,633
Not yet. I stayed up all night
to watch over Gabo.

314
00:16:17,633 --> 00:16:19,167
Did he catch a fever?

315
00:16:19,667 --> 00:16:21,133
Thankfully, no.

316
00:16:21,667 --> 00:16:23,500
[RUDY] If I see those bastards
on the street,

317
00:16:23,500 --> 00:16:25,200
I'll hack them all to pieces!

318
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:26,300
[HUFFING]

319
00:16:26,300 --> 00:16:27,933
Say what now? Hack them?

320
00:16:27,933 --> 00:16:29,033
Hey, hey, hey!

321
00:16:29,033 --> 00:16:32,000
We've got enough problems.
Don't add to them!

322
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:33,900
[DANTE] I woke up early today,

323
00:16:33,900 --> 00:16:36,633
and someone told me that
the people Gabo ran into

324
00:16:36,633 --> 00:16:37,800
are still here.

325
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:39,300
- Huh?
- They're still here?

326
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:40,367
Whoa, whoa!

327
00:16:40,367 --> 00:16:41,600
Listen up!

328
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:42,800
You're both staying put!

329
00:16:42,833 --> 00:16:44,400
Nobody leaves!

330
00:16:44,900 --> 00:16:48,267
Alright, I'm going to cook
breakfast now.

331
00:16:48,267 --> 00:16:49,933
Dante, help me.

332
00:16:49,933 --> 00:16:54,400
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

333
00:16:54,400 --> 00:16:55,433
Gloria.

334
00:16:56,000 --> 00:17:00,033
Thank you so much
for taking care of Gabo.

335
00:17:00,433 --> 00:17:01,800
It's no big deal, sir.

336
00:17:02,233 --> 00:17:05,067
I'm just doing
my part as his wife.

337
00:17:05,067 --> 00:17:06,733
[RUDY] Gabo is one lucky man.

338
00:17:07,400 --> 00:17:08,933
Because you're his wife.

339
00:17:10,033 --> 00:17:11,467
- [EXHALES SOFTLY]
- [RUDY SIGHS]

340
00:17:12,767 --> 00:17:14,067
I-I'll head out for a bit.

341
00:17:14,067 --> 00:17:15,267
Please look after him.

342
00:17:16,333 --> 00:17:23,300
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

343
00:17:24,033 --> 00:17:25,533
- [DANTE] Hey, Rudy.
- Oh?

344
00:17:25,533 --> 00:17:27,100
- I have something to tell you.
- Come on, let's eat.

345
00:17:27,100 --> 00:17:28,567
- What is it?
- About Gloria.

346
00:17:28,900 --> 00:17:30,300
- Alright, spill.
- I'm impressed.

347
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:32,267
She kept guard outside
last night,

348
00:17:32,267 --> 00:17:35,267
and now she's inside their room
watching over Gabo.

349
00:17:35,733 --> 00:17:39,033
[MAMENG] What? What if Gabo's
enemies suddenly showed up?

350
00:17:39,033 --> 00:17:40,733
- Right.
- Could she even handle them?

351
00:17:40,733 --> 00:17:42,700
Could she really fight them off,

352
00:17:42,700 --> 00:17:44,267
especially since
they're all men?

353
00:17:44,267 --> 00:17:46,300
From what I can see in Gloria,

354
00:17:46,300 --> 00:17:48,933
she's capable
of protecting Gabo.

355
00:17:48,967 --> 00:17:50,000
[RUDY] You know what?

356
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:51,800
- I get the feeling...
- [DANTE] Hmm?

357
00:17:52,233 --> 00:17:53,767
Gloria's fallen for Gabo.

358
00:17:53,767 --> 00:17:55,233
Just a reminder.

359
00:17:55,733 --> 00:17:57,667
This is all an act.

360
00:17:57,667 --> 00:17:59,033
- That's right.
- Remember?

361
00:17:59,033 --> 00:18:00,200
[SAM INHALES DEEPLY]

362
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:07,133
[TENDER MUSIC PLAYING]

363
00:18:09,733 --> 00:18:13,200
[SAM] <i> I hope you feel better
</i> when you wake up.

364
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:15,967
<i> Don't worry, Gabo.</i>

365
00:18:17,033 --> 00:18:18,867
<i> I'll make it up to you.</i>

366
00:18:20,567 --> 00:18:22,733
<i>This time,
I'll take care of you.</i>

367
00:18:22,767 --> 00:18:28,233
[TENDER MUSIC CONTINUES]

368
00:18:30,967 --> 00:18:35,433
You're already retired,
General Ricardo Jacinto.

369
00:18:35,433 --> 00:18:39,500
<i>But you're still using
your influence in the NLEA</i>

370
00:18:39,500 --> 00:18:42,933
<i>to get what you want.
I'm right, aren't I?</i>

371
00:18:42,933 --> 00:18:48,267
<i>You're the one
who had Victor Zafra transferred</i>

372
00:18:48,267 --> 00:18:51,200
<i> to help your daughter...</i>

373
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:55,367
<i>...who is assigned
in the NCIA.</i>

374
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:58,500
<i>If you think
I'm just making noise,</i>

375
00:18:58,500 --> 00:19:00,567
<i> well, I won't stop</i>

376
00:19:00,567 --> 00:19:06,367
<i>until every crooked person
like you is gone!</i>

377
00:19:06,367 --> 00:19:07,733
<i> Huh? Huh?!</i>

378
00:19:07,733 --> 00:19:10,667
Is this damn reporter
still not stopping?

379
00:19:10,667 --> 00:19:13,367
Well, who told him
that General Jacinto

380
00:19:13,367 --> 00:19:15,700
had something to do
with transferring the gold?

381
00:19:15,700 --> 00:19:16,967
Me.

382
00:19:16,967 --> 00:19:19,367
I mentioned that General Jacinto

383
00:19:19,367 --> 00:19:21,800
had Victor Zafra's
transfer expedited.

384
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:24,367
Still, the media shouldn't have
taken malice into it.

385
00:19:24,367 --> 00:19:28,167
As you know, sir,
every NLEA general who retired

386
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:29,467
still has influence in here.

387
00:19:29,467 --> 00:19:34,333
They still should not know
what happened to Sam Jacinto.

388
00:19:34,333 --> 00:19:35,633
If news of that breaks out,

389
00:19:35,633 --> 00:19:37,167
they'll ambush us
with questions.

390
00:19:38,167 --> 00:19:39,167
Yes, sir.

391
00:19:41,067 --> 00:19:42,167
[RICARDO CHUCKLES]

392
00:19:42,767 --> 00:19:44,600
That reporter...

393
00:19:44,667 --> 00:19:48,467
It's obvious he's using you
to make a name for himself.

394
00:19:48,467 --> 00:19:49,967
He won't stop attacking me.

395
00:19:50,567 --> 00:19:53,933
Why doesn't he report
about the corrupt politicians?

396
00:19:54,600 --> 00:19:56,433
Those are the real enemies
of his audience!

397
00:19:57,000 --> 00:20:00,200
What do you want us to do?
Want to get back at him?

398
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:03,633
But if we do that,
it might cause more trouble.

399
00:20:03,667 --> 00:20:04,867
Even if he makes a ruckus...

400
00:20:05,600 --> 00:20:08,133
Even if he sues me,
I'll face him.

401
00:20:08,133 --> 00:20:10,400
I'll make that Salvador pay.

402
00:20:13,700 --> 00:20:14,733
[ISOBEL INHALES]

403
00:20:16,567 --> 00:20:18,800
Madam Rosa, can we start?

404
00:20:19,367 --> 00:20:21,133
I got so drained
from the traffic.

405
00:20:21,133 --> 00:20:23,367
- Can I eat for a while?
- Ah.

406
00:20:26,700 --> 00:20:29,767
- Want me to clean this up?
- No, no. Leave it there.

407
00:20:32,267 --> 00:20:33,600
- [CUTLERY CLINKS]
- Come on.

408
00:20:33,600 --> 00:20:35,700
This is it. Come on.
Let's get started.

409
00:20:35,733 --> 00:20:37,533
You keep rushing me.

410
00:20:37,533 --> 00:20:39,667
You know, Madam Rosa
also gets stressed.

411
00:20:39,667 --> 00:20:41,900
- Oh, sorry. I'm sorry.
- Shush!

412
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:43,567
Let's start.

413
00:20:43,567 --> 00:20:45,000
[ROSA CLEARS THROAT]

414
00:20:48,233 --> 00:20:49,467
[ROSA HUMS]

415
00:20:50,433 --> 00:20:55,333
[ROSA HUMMING]

416
00:20:55,333 --> 00:20:58,933
[ROSA HUMMING, MOANING]

417
00:20:59,700 --> 00:21:05,367
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

418
00:21:05,367 --> 00:21:06,667
[EGG CRACKS]

419
00:21:06,667 --> 00:21:12,833
[ROSA GASPS, GROANS]

420
00:21:12,867 --> 00:21:15,133
Madam Rosa, do you see her?

421
00:21:15,133 --> 00:21:17,567
- [ROSA CRIES]
- What do you see?

422
00:21:17,567 --> 00:21:20,267
- Have you seen anything?
- Not yet.

423
00:21:20,267 --> 00:21:22,800
- Oh, not yet. My God.
- Again, again.

424
00:21:22,800 --> 00:21:28,867
[ROSA SINGING A CHANT]

425
00:21:28,867 --> 00:21:33,633
No! No! Stop that! Stop that!

426
00:21:33,633 --> 00:21:35,433
Please have mercy, stop that!

427
00:21:35,433 --> 00:21:37,400
Madam Rosa, what happened
to my daughter?

428
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:40,167
[ROSA BREATHING HEAVILY]

429
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:44,467
What-- What happened
to my daughter?

430
00:21:44,467 --> 00:21:47,500
Tell me what happened
to Sam.

431
00:21:48,633 --> 00:21:51,567
- The cards have to confirm it.
- Is that so?

432
00:21:51,567 --> 00:21:53,600
Pick three. Pick.

433
00:21:53,600 --> 00:21:57,000
I said three, just three.
Don't look at it.

434
00:21:57,867 --> 00:21:59,000
I don't--

435
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:00,300
[ROSA GROANS]

436
00:22:00,300 --> 00:22:04,267
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

437
00:22:04,267 --> 00:22:06,267
Ten of swords.

438
00:22:07,933 --> 00:22:09,400
Tower. [GASPS]

439
00:22:11,667 --> 00:22:15,533
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

440
00:22:15,567 --> 00:22:18,067
- Death.
- Death?

441
00:22:18,067 --> 00:22:21,400
Madam Rosa now knows
the truth, Isobel.

442
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:25,200
What happened to my daughter?
I want to know.

443
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:28,533
Sam suffered tragically, Isobel!

444
00:22:28,533 --> 00:22:31,300
Don't tell me,
don't say that.

445
00:22:31,300 --> 00:22:35,833
Sam was stabbed!
She was stabbed repeatedly!

446
00:22:35,833 --> 00:22:38,467
They chopped up her body!

447
00:22:38,467 --> 00:22:40,667
- [ISOBEL CRYING]
- They're so cruel!

448
00:22:40,667 --> 00:22:43,800
They put her inside
a drum, Isobel.

449
00:22:43,800 --> 00:22:47,367
They put her inside
a drum, Isobel! A drum!

450
00:22:47,367 --> 00:22:51,733
They threw it somewhere
far away in Manila Bay!

451
00:22:51,767 --> 00:22:55,067
No! No! Sam!

452
00:22:55,067 --> 00:22:56,400
[ISOBEL CRYING]

453
00:22:56,400 --> 00:22:58,933
- Isobel!
- Sam!

454
00:22:58,933 --> 00:23:01,900
Your daughter
Sam's heart stopped

455
00:23:01,900 --> 00:23:04,233
the same time
this watch stopped!

456
00:23:04,233 --> 00:23:08,267
This watch is useless now,
Isobel.

457
00:23:08,267 --> 00:23:11,433
This is useless
because your daughter's gone!

458
00:23:11,433 --> 00:23:15,867
- [ISOBEL CRYING]
- Isobel, Sam is gone!

459
00:23:15,867 --> 00:23:17,433
[ISOBEL CRYING]

460
00:23:17,433 --> 00:23:18,533
This is Sam.

461
00:23:18,533 --> 00:23:20,367
[ISOBEL BREATHES]

462
00:23:20,367 --> 00:23:26,067
[WAILING] Sam! No! Sam!

463
00:23:26,100 --> 00:23:27,367
[ISOBEL CRYING]

464
00:23:27,367 --> 00:23:34,033
Sam! My daughter's not dead!
No! No! No!

465
00:23:34,033 --> 00:23:35,133
[ISOBEL CRYING]

466
00:23:35,133 --> 00:23:36,433
[PINKY] Madam Rosa!

467
00:23:36,433 --> 00:23:38,500
- What's happening?
- Sam's dead!

468
00:23:38,500 --> 00:23:41,133
- Isobel! Isobel.
- [PINKY] Isobel, calm down.

469
00:23:41,133 --> 00:23:43,133
- What's wrong?
- [PINKY] Calm down, Isobel.

470
00:23:43,133 --> 00:23:45,067
Our daughter is dead!

471
00:23:45,067 --> 00:23:48,933
The fortune teller said
her body was stabbed,

472
00:23:48,933 --> 00:23:51,667
placed inside a drum,
and thrown into the water!

473
00:23:51,667 --> 00:23:53,700
- Are you crazy?
- [PINKY] Isobel.

474
00:23:53,700 --> 00:23:55,367
[RICARDO]
Our daughter is not dead!

475
00:23:55,400 --> 00:23:59,067
- [PINKY] Isobel.
- [ISOBEL] No, no, my youngest!

476
00:23:59,067 --> 00:24:00,967
- Stop it.
- [ISOBEL CRYING]

477
00:24:00,967 --> 00:24:03,767
Toto, get her out of here.
Get her out!

478
00:24:03,767 --> 00:24:05,833
Come on. Let's get you out.

479
00:24:05,833 --> 00:24:07,267
- [ISOBEL CRYING]
- Get out.

480
00:24:07,267 --> 00:24:08,833
- You have to accept it.
- Stop it.

481
00:24:08,833 --> 00:24:11,233
I'm not lying.
You have to face the truth!

482
00:24:11,233 --> 00:24:13,667
- [RICARDO] Get out!
- [ROSA] My cards don't lie!

483
00:24:13,667 --> 00:24:16,767
I can't take it, Sam!

484
00:24:16,767 --> 00:24:20,967
I can't take it! I can't!

485
00:24:23,500 --> 00:24:24,633
[TEKLA] Uncle Rudy?

486
00:24:24,633 --> 00:24:26,767
- Uncle Rudy, how's Gabo?
- Hey!

487
00:24:26,767 --> 00:24:28,333
- Is Gabo okay now?
- Gabo...

488
00:24:28,333 --> 00:24:29,867
Where is he?

489
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:32,433
- Hey!
- Shh!

490
00:24:32,433 --> 00:24:36,067
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

491
00:24:36,067 --> 00:24:37,300
Maybe he got amnesia, too.

492
00:24:37,300 --> 00:24:39,467
- Just like Gloria.
- Hey, come on.

493
00:24:39,467 --> 00:24:41,900
- Oh no.
- He's right.

494
00:24:41,900 --> 00:24:44,700
Hey, hey, hey!
Can you guys keep it down?

495
00:24:44,700 --> 00:24:47,133
- They might hear us.
- He said be quiet.

496
00:24:48,933 --> 00:24:50,200
Wait, wait.

497
00:24:50,200 --> 00:24:51,567
What's the news outside?

498
00:24:51,567 --> 00:24:54,767
There are still armed men
all over the place,

499
00:24:54,767 --> 00:24:57,033
but you can't really tell
because they're blending in.

500
00:24:57,033 --> 00:24:58,733
They're definitely looking
for someone.

501
00:24:58,733 --> 00:24:59,900
It's your fault!

502
00:24:59,900 --> 00:25:02,967
Why did you agree
to hide that woman here?

503
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:05,633
Look at what happened.
Gabo got hurt because of her!

504
00:25:06,400 --> 00:25:08,033
That woman really gets
on my nerves.

505
00:25:08,033 --> 00:25:09,567
- Shh!
- Tekla!

506
00:25:10,700 --> 00:25:13,500
Gloria was the one
who took care of Gabo.

507
00:25:13,500 --> 00:25:15,633
Wow! Are we supposed
to praise her now?

508
00:25:15,633 --> 00:25:16,800
I can do that!

509
00:25:16,800 --> 00:25:18,267
I've been doing it
for a long time.

510
00:25:18,267 --> 00:25:20,633
I can take care of him
way better than she can.

511
00:25:20,633 --> 00:25:23,133
Look at you, you're so jealous.

512
00:25:23,133 --> 00:25:24,867
Gabo and Gloria
are together now.

513
00:25:24,867 --> 00:25:26,533
Come on. They're married.

514
00:25:26,533 --> 00:25:28,767
Hey, hold on, Uncle Dante.
What do you mean, married?

515
00:25:28,767 --> 00:25:31,033
Are we all forgetting

516
00:25:31,033 --> 00:25:32,933
that we're just going along
with their act

517
00:25:32,933 --> 00:25:34,800
- of pretending to be married?
- Shh!

518
00:25:34,800 --> 00:25:36,867
- Shh. Will you stop it?
- Why?

519
00:25:36,900 --> 00:25:40,300
- Gloria might hear you!
- Well, good! Let her hear it!

520
00:25:40,300 --> 00:25:42,933
- Shh!
- [MAMENG] Wait.

521
00:25:42,933 --> 00:25:46,333
We might as well all eat.

522
00:25:46,333 --> 00:25:47,867
Yeah, Miss Betchay
might come back.

523
00:25:47,867 --> 00:25:50,100
- [DABOY] I'm starving.
- I can tell.

524
00:25:50,100 --> 00:25:52,100
- Move.
- Miss Betchay might come back.

525
00:25:54,400 --> 00:25:56,767
- [GABO GROANS]
- Honey?

526
00:25:56,767 --> 00:25:58,467
Hey, wait.

527
00:25:58,467 --> 00:25:59,933
Wait, don't move yet.

528
00:25:59,933 --> 00:26:01,500
You might hurt yourself.

529
00:26:02,133 --> 00:26:04,567
[GABO GROANING]

530
00:26:04,567 --> 00:26:06,833
[GABO BREATHING HEAVILY]

531
00:26:06,833 --> 00:26:08,533
What? Does your body hurt?

532
00:26:08,567 --> 00:26:12,433
[GABO BREATHING HEAVILY]

533
00:26:16,067 --> 00:26:17,233
What happened?

534
00:26:18,167 --> 00:26:20,567
Your friends brought you here
last night.

535
00:26:20,567 --> 00:26:22,333
They said you ran
into your enemies,

536
00:26:22,333 --> 00:26:24,100
and someone hit you
on the head,

537
00:26:24,100 --> 00:26:25,933
so you passed out.

538
00:26:25,933 --> 00:26:27,500
I told you.

539
00:26:27,500 --> 00:26:29,300
You shouldn't have left.

540
00:26:29,800 --> 00:26:31,800
What if something
happened to you?

541
00:26:31,800 --> 00:26:34,467
What if you got shot?
What if you died?

542
00:26:34,467 --> 00:26:36,100
I wouldn't have known
what to do.

543
00:26:37,233 --> 00:26:44,067
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
INSTRUMENTAL PLAYING]

544
00:26:45,900 --> 00:26:47,100
Gloria.

545
00:26:51,767 --> 00:26:52,967
I'm sorry, okay?

546
00:26:54,867 --> 00:26:56,500
I know I was being stubborn.

547
00:26:58,867 --> 00:27:00,367
But don't worry.

548
00:27:01,933 --> 00:27:04,333
I promise nothing bad's
going to happen to me.

549
00:27:05,567 --> 00:27:07,133
I'm not dying yet.

550
00:27:08,867 --> 00:27:10,700
I couldn't bear to leave you.

551
00:27:11,967 --> 00:27:15,267
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
CONTINUES]

552
00:27:15,800 --> 00:27:18,200
Promise me you won't
do that again, okay?

553
00:27:20,367 --> 00:27:21,533
I'm thankful...

554
00:27:23,600 --> 00:27:25,733
that God gave me
another chance to live.

555
00:27:27,833 --> 00:27:28,900
For you.

556
00:27:29,300 --> 00:27:36,133
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
CONTINUES]

557
00:27:39,833 --> 00:27:41,833
[GABO] I won't let you get hurt.

558
00:27:41,833 --> 00:27:44,567
<i>I'll do whatever it takes
to protect you, Gloria.</i>

559
00:27:44,567 --> 00:27:46,700
<i> I'll risk my life for you.</i>

560
00:27:47,433 --> 00:27:49,767
[SAM] <i> I'm probably
</i> taking my acting

561
00:27:50,567 --> 00:27:52,600
<i> as Gabo's wife too far.</i>

562
00:27:53,367 --> 00:27:56,133
<i> Am I going too far?</i>

563
00:27:57,900 --> 00:27:59,067
<i> No.</i>

564
00:27:59,067 --> 00:28:00,167
<i> This is just right.</i>

565
00:28:00,667 --> 00:28:03,367
<i>So they won't sense anything
or notice how I'm acting.</i>

566
00:28:04,167 --> 00:28:08,600
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
CONTINUES]

567
00:28:11,533 --> 00:28:12,533
Honey.

568
00:28:12,533 --> 00:28:14,033
Where are Papa and the others?

569
00:28:15,367 --> 00:28:16,833
They're in the kitchen.

570
00:28:17,567 --> 00:28:19,433
I'll go see them for a bit.

571
00:28:19,433 --> 00:28:21,400
- Can you manage?
- I can.

572
00:28:22,533 --> 00:28:24,200
- Careful.
- I'm okay.

573
00:28:26,400 --> 00:28:27,900
Don't worry about me anymore.

574
00:28:31,967 --> 00:28:33,133
[GROANS]

575
00:28:41,400 --> 00:28:42,467
Pa?

576
00:28:42,467 --> 00:28:43,900
- It's Gabo!
- It's Gabo!

577
00:28:43,900 --> 00:28:45,667
- Move! Move!
- He can walk on his own.

578
00:28:45,667 --> 00:28:47,200
- Hey!
- You're so dramatic!

579
00:28:47,267 --> 00:28:49,467
- Gabo, are you okay?
- It hurts! It hurts!

580
00:28:49,467 --> 00:28:50,533
Hold on to me.

581
00:28:50,533 --> 00:28:53,133
I'll take care of you.
I'll massage you.

582
00:28:53,133 --> 00:28:55,300
I'll be the one to
take care of you.

583
00:28:55,300 --> 00:28:57,333
- Tekla!
- Get that woman out of here.

584
00:28:57,367 --> 00:28:58,833
- Shh.
- Sit down, Gabo.

585
00:28:58,833 --> 00:29:01,333
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

586
00:29:01,333 --> 00:29:03,733
<i>What if the people who want
to kill me are still out there?</i>

587
00:29:07,233 --> 00:29:10,033
<i>What if they find out
I'm still here with Gabo?</i>

588
00:29:11,767 --> 00:29:13,900
<i>What if they discover
I'm hiding here?</i>

589
00:29:13,900 --> 00:29:18,633
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

590
00:29:18,633 --> 00:29:20,133
<i> I have to be prepared.</i>

591
00:29:21,067 --> 00:29:23,033
<i>I can't let them catch me
off guard.</i>

592
00:29:23,967 --> 00:29:26,200
<i>Before they even get
to this house,</i>

593
00:29:29,000 --> 00:29:30,667
<i> I'll be ready for them.</i>

594
00:29:32,833 --> 00:29:35,967
<i>- What do you want to happen?
- I want something to happen!</i>

595
00:29:35,967 --> 00:29:37,867
<i>We're taking too long
to find Ma'am Sam!</i>

596
00:29:37,867 --> 00:29:40,033
<i>- What are you doing here?
- We were invited.</i>

597
00:29:40,033 --> 00:29:43,933
<i>We need to get back the gold
the NLEA took from us.</i>

598
00:29:43,933 --> 00:29:48,333
And you, Lucas,
will lead this operation.

599
00:29:48,333 --> 00:29:49,700
<i> Betchay is all about money,</i>

600
00:29:49,700 --> 00:29:51,333
<i>so she'll be the first one
we approach.</i>

601
00:29:51,400 --> 00:29:54,233
<i>We're here again to try
to settle this</i>

602
00:29:54,233 --> 00:29:56,000
<i> and offer our assistance.</i>

603
00:29:56,067 --> 00:29:57,467
<i>I'll find out,
one way or another,</i>

604
00:29:57,467 --> 00:30:01,033
<i>which cops shot me
on Ricardo Jacinto's orders!</i>

605
00:30:01,033 --> 00:30:03,500
<i>So I'll know who to
press charges against!</i>

606
00:30:03,533 --> 00:30:06,100
My father won't agree to this,
and we won't accept your money!

607
00:30:06,100 --> 00:30:08,567
<i>And if possible, we don't want
to see your faces here again.</i>

608
00:30:08,567 --> 00:30:11,167
<i>Once you sign this,
you'll lose your land.</i>

609
00:30:11,167 --> 00:30:13,867
<i>Those aren't real NGOs.
They're just fooling us!</i>
